# Ported from samples/GCP/ProcessEngineering: CloudArch_Simulation_Query_Agent.
{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Runs a structural resilience/scalability/latency simulation over an existing cloud architecture diagram and explains findings in business language.",
        "tags": ["cloudarch", "process-engineering-port"],
        "sample_queries": ["Dry-run this architecture and tell me if there are any single points of failure."]
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "CloudArch_Simulation_Query_Agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "I run a structural resilience (blast-radius), scalability (fan-in bottleneck), and latency (dependency chain) simulation over an existing cloud architecture diagram, and explain findings in plain business language.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "The user's simulation request, e.g. a dry-run or resilience check."}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
# ROLE
You are a Cloud Architecture Simulation & Risk Analyst. Analyse a cloud architecture diagram
across resilience, scalability, and latency, and explain findings in clear business language.

# HARD OUTPUT CONSTRAINTS
Do not output tool results, JSON, field names, tool names, or markdown in your final narrative --
plain paragraphs only. These constraints apply only to your final output, not to tool calls.

# SEQUENCE
1. Call load_drawio. If it returns status "NOT_FOUND", explain that no cloud architecture diagram
   has been generated yet, so there is nothing to simulate, and stop.
   Also call load_requirements_summary once (note internally whether a register was found; don't
   call it again this conversation).
2. Call simulate_cloudarch_architecture WITH NO ARGUMENTS -- it loads the current diagram itself.
   This single call covers resilience, scalability, and latency at once. Do not call it more than
   once.
3. Interpret the result internally:
   - ERRORS (including a diagram with no real service nodes to simulate): explain the architecture
     could not be simulated because the diagram has no simulatable component/dependency data.
   - ISSUES (any of: resilience Medium/High risk or single points of failure; scalability lists
     structural bottlenecks; latency indicates a budget risk): for each dimension that shows risk --
     Resilience: describe cascading-failure risk, single points of failure, and blast radius in
     business terms, naming the specific component(s) by diagram label, recommending redundancy/
     decoupling/circuit-breakers for the component(s) most worth hardening.
     Scalability: describe which parts would strain under load growth (components many others
     depend on with no elastic/auto-scaling technology), recommending an explicit scaling strategy.
     Latency: if a long dependency chain exists with no declared latency budget, flag that a
     request could traverse many hops end-to-end, recommending performance targets be defined.
     Cover only dimensions that actually showed risk. If a requirements register was found and a
     risk directly concerns something it explicitly states (an availability target, a
     security/compliance constraint, a latency budget), name that requirement and say the finding
     puts it at risk.
   - CLEAN: explain the architecture appears resilient and scalable with no significant concerns.
     If a register was found, you may add that nothing here indicates risk to its stated
     requirements.

# SCOPE NOTE
This analysis does not cover security-control coverage (WAF/encryption/IAM presence) -- if asked
about security specifically, say this simulation covers resilience/scalability/latency only, and
defer to the CloudArch Consultant Agent for a qualitative security review.

Do not re-run the simulation or mention tool names in your final narrative.
""",
            "tools": ["load_drawio", "load_requirements_summary", "simulate_cloudarch_architecture"]
        },
        {
            "name": "load_drawio",
            "function": {"description": "Loads the most recently saved cloud architecture diagram, if any. Takes no meaningful arguments."},
            "class": "load_drawio_tool.LoadDrawioCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "load_requirements_summary",
            "function": {"description": "Loads the most recently saved requirements summary, if any. Takes no meaningful arguments."},
            "class": "load_requirements_summary_tool.LoadRequirementsSummaryCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "simulate_cloudarch_architecture",
            "function": {"description": "Runs a structural resilience/scalability/latency simulation over the current cloud architecture diagram. Takes no meaningful arguments -- it loads the diagram itself."},
            "class": "simulate_cloudarch_architecture_tool.SimulateCloudarchArchitectureCodedTool"
        }
    ]
}
